Arpan","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-06T07:25:15.202Z","text":"RBI tomorrow: 25 or 50 bps? Is the Fed forcing our hand again? — Shhh , dont let the FII’s know , lets the puts come down a bit","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/rbi-tomorrow-25-or-50-bps-is-the-fed-forcing-our-hand-again/198588/8","sentiment":"neutral","likes":0,"comments":0,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-06T14:11:05.297Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-14T22:38:30.450Z"},{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-542001","source":"tradingqna","author":"BB789","handle":"@BB789","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:56:27.113Z","text":"RBI tomorrow: 25 or 50 bps? Is the Fed forcing our hand again? — Isn’t that already known and priced in?","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/rbi-tomorrow-25-or-50-bps-is-the-fed-forcing-our-hand-again/198588/7","sentiment":"neutral","likes":0,"comments":1,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-06T14:11:05.297Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-14T22:38:30.450Z"},{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-541999","source":"tradingqna","author":"amitskale","handle":"@amitskale","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:47:47.127Z","text":"RBI tomorrow: 25 or 50 bps? Is the Fed forcing our hand again? — If u mean bond markets then they are going to react negatively to this and yields will rise further.. Rise in bond yields are generally negative for the stock market","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/rbi-tomorrow-25-or-50-bps-is-the-fed-forcing-our-hand-again/198588/6","sentiment":"neutral","likes":1,"comments":0,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-06T06:52:05.631Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-14T22:38:30.450Z"},{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-541997","source":"tradingqna","author":"Arpan","handle":"@Arpan","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:41:42.225Z","text":"RBI tomorrow: 25 or 50 bps? Is the Fed forcing our hand again? — Crash, Market will think RBI is compromised","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/rbi-tomorrow-25-or-50-bps-is-the-fed-forcing-our-hand-again/198588/5","sentiment":"bearish","likes":2,"comments":1,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-06T06:52:05.631Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-14T22:38:30.450Z"},{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-541992","source":"tradingqna","author":"Danny_Crespin","handle":"@Danny_Crespin","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:27:43.958Z","text":"RBI tomorrow: 25 or 50 bps? Is the Fed forcing our hand again? — where do you think the market will go if no rate hike is done?","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/rbi-tomorrow-25-or-50-bps-is-the-fed-forcing-our-hand-again/198588/4","sentiment":"neutral","likes":0,"comments":2,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-06T06:52:05.631Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-14T22:38:30.450Z"},{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-541987","source":"tradingqna","author":"amitskale","handle":"@amitskale","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-06T06:05:35.146Z","text":"RBI tomorrow: 25 or 50 bps? Is the Fed forcing our hand again? — 50 bps is the right thing to do but looking at their pro govt stance they will do 25 bps and keep the commentary as well neutral when ideally it should be hawkish. I wouldn’t be surprised if they even don’t raise the rates at all tomorrow because they are in a denial mode all the time that inflation is higher and rather will have audacity to say that current inflation is supply side and that’s why rate increase is not warranted..","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/rbi-tomorrow-25-or-50-bps-is-the-fed-forcing-our-hand-again/198588/3","sentiment":"neutral","likes":3,"comments":1,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-06T06:52:05.631Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-14T22:38:30.450Z"},{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-541976","source":"tradingqna","author":"BB789","handle":"@BB789","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-06T04:46:21.411Z","text":"RBI tomorrow: 25 or 50 bps? Is the Fed forcing our hand again? — 50 would be good, but IMO, RBI don’t have the guts to do that.","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/rbi-tomorrow-25-or-50-bps-is-the-fed-forcing-our-hand-again/198588/2","sentiment":"neutral","likes":3,"comments":0,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-06T06:52:05.631Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-14T22:38:30.450Z"},{"id":"tradingqna-tqna-541974","source":"tradingqna","author":"Danny_Crespin","handle":"@Danny_Crespin","community":"TradingQnA","timestamp":"2026-10-06T04:35:29.957Z","text":"RBI tomorrow: 25 or 50 bps? Is the Fed forcing our hand again? — MPC decision is out tomorrow at 10 am. Consensus is a 25 bps hike, taking repo to 5.50%. My view: the repo rate isn’t a tool to attract FIIs, but sometimes the RBI is forced to react to the Fed. US 10Y is above 5.2% and ours is at 7.21%, so the spread is only about 200 bps. That’s thin for anyone carrying rupee risk. Capital leaves, the rupee weakens, and with Brent still around $100 that feeds into inflation. We’ve seen this before. In 2013 the RBI pushed MSF up 200 bps to defend the rupee, and in May 2022 it did an off-cycle hi…","url":"https://tradingqna.com/t/rbi-tomorrow-25-or-50-bps-is-the-fed-forcing-our-hand-again/198588/1","sentiment":"neutral","likes":1,"comments":0,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-06T06:52:05.631Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-14T22:38:30.450Z"},{"id":"news-gn-NMXhBLV9jWEFQMG9Za2xUeUtZeXdnYWs","source":"news","author":"Reuters","handle":"Reuters","community":"Google News","timestamp":"2026-10-05T17:58:40.000Z","text":"Indian shares rise as oil, Fed fears ease; financials gain on Q2 updates","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxOU25TQndoMFZ0ZFhnN2QyYjVvel9GQ2pLUnpmOThYRml6eWtoZ2lCNEJUMTlCTHhRbVZDNXVxeUpsR1phdmFDN3g5cGNKa09ialV0TzVqNElNT0Z1OGlxZ2pOQ0g2VGFoVExXQTVrRkNtVS02bV9TZVFmcGJ0V29jWjBTX3RmNHRWRThjWG9FODRqWHJNMXhBLV9jWEFQMG9Za2xUeUtZeXdnYWs?oc=5","sentiment":"neutral","likes":0,"comments":0,"firstSeenAt":"2026-10-05T18:26:23.873Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-11T23:10:32.260Z"},{"id":"news-gn-w0VG1kMHJCcUFKRUJEZ2ZEaUI4aWIwQQ","source":"news","author":"Investing.com","handle":"Investing.com","community":"Google News","timestamp":"2026-10-05T01:41:15.000Z","text":"Stocks upbeat, dollar wobbles as Fed hike bets recede By Reuters","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipwFBVV95cUxPLV9uWU